/* Grid-table STRUCTURE (Format-Table style) — applied by Format-Styled for multi-object /
 * -Table output, layered ON TOP of the semantic sheet (default.css or a user -Css). It sets
 * only structure — header weight/rule, primary-column weight, numeric alignment — and never
 * sets colour on data cells, so the semantic sheet's Kind/class colours win on the data.
 *
 * Cell classes the cmdlet assigns:
 *   .header   first (header) row — one cell per property name
 *   .primary  the first data column (the object's key/name) on every row
 *   .num      header + data cells of a numeric column (right-aligned)
 *   .cell     every data cell (left for user targeting; intentionally unstyled here)
 *
 * CUSTOMIZE: drop a `table.css` into $PSBASH_STYLE_PATH, ~/.config/ps-bash/styles, or
 * ~/.psbash/styles; your rules are appended after these (later declarations win).
 */

.header  { font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline }
.primary { font-weight: bold }
.num     { text-align: right }
